    "body": "- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\nNeeded this to avoid orchestrating my other floats around the default 10 z-index. [nvim-treesitter-context](https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-context) has a default of 20 so anyone installing it would run into this issue.\r\n\r\nI'm currently using a [fork](https://github.com/nolantait/mini.map) of this on my [configs](https://github.com/nolantait/dotfiles/blob/a0c754859046d513ea6c0ce7ee89b74e4b839f8c/config/nvim/lua/plugins/configs/mini-map.lua#L43) and its working great.\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2023-10-19T11:53:26Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the contribution!\r\n\r\nI kind of regret not having the whole `config` overridable (like was somewhat established in later modules). At the same time, I don't really want to open the door to all available `nvim_open_win()` options.\r\n\r\nI'll think about addressing this. Here are possible solutions that come to my head right now:\r\n- Export `MiniMapOpened` and `MiniMapClosed` `User` events to allow users to customize inside autocommand.\r\n- Move `window.focusable` and `window.width` to `window.config.focusable` and `window.config.width`, while allowing to override whole `window.config`. This is breaking change, but of course with some period of backwards compatibility.\r\n- Add `zindex` as in this PR in hope that this will be enough for the future.",
            "created_at": "2023-10-16T08:13:46Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/520#issuecomment-1763957307",
            "id": 1763957307,
